INT. NEON ARENA - MAIN STAGE - NIGHT

BOOM. Lights slam on. Ten thousand fans ROAR.

ANGLE ON a glowing stage, two gaming rigs, a giant screen counting down from ten.

Ava, 12, sits at the left rig, headset crooked, knuckles white.

AVA
(cracking her fingers, eyes locked on the screen)
Ten seconds, Dad. Ten.

Her father Ray, 40s, crouches at her side with a water bottle and a sweat-soaked T-shirt.

RAY
(handing her the bottle, jaw tight)
Breathe, Ava. Breathe, kiddo. You've got this.

BEEP. BEEP. BEEP.

CLOSE ON Ava's thumbs, hovering over the controller.

On the giant screen: GAME START.

AVA
(hammering the buttons)
Left flank! Left flank! Where's Grandpa?!

INSERT - PHONE SCREEN: "GRANDPA WALT CALLING."

Ray's phone BUZZES on the desk. He swipes it open and props it against the monitor.

WALT (V.O.)
(crackling, from the phone)
Is she winning? Tell me she's winning. I've got the whole bingo hall watching!

RAY
(shouting over the crowd)
She's winning, Dad! She's down to the last round!

BACK TO SCENE.

On the right rig: the rival, a hooded STRANGER, face lit blue by the screen, fingers a blur.

STRANGER
(muttering)
Not today, little one.

KRAKOOM. Sparks erupt across the big screen. The crowd GASPS.

AVA
(jaw clenched)
Dad, he's got the golden shield!

RAY
(leaning in)
So take it from him!

AVA
(typing, teeth bared)
I'm trying!

WE SEE the Stranger's screen mirror Ava's: two avatars, one mountain, one flag.

WALT (V.O.)
(yelling)
Ava! Remember what I taught you! Duck and weave!

AVA
(not looking away)
It's a video game, Grandpa, not boxing!

WHAM. The Stranger's avatar knocks hers back a step.

STRANGER
(peeling off his hood, grinning, suddenly kind)
Nice one, kid. I'm Marcus, by the way. Marcus Bell. I played your dad back in the day.

RAY
(stunned, half-rising)
Marcus?! You're THE Marcus?!

MARCUS
(still tapping, easy)
Yep. Still got the reflexes.

AVA
(furious, tapping faster)
Dad! Don't talk to the enemy!

RAY
(sitting back down fast)
Sorry! Sorry, kiddo, focus!

CLOSE ON the countdown: 00:09. 00:08. 00:07.

WALT (V.O.)
(from the phone, crackling)
Seven seconds! Go, go, GO!

CRASH. The big screen explodes in light.
